export default [
{slug:'scientific-calculator-degrees-sin-log-factorial',title:'Use a scientific calculator in degrees: sin, powers, logs and factorials',category:'learning',date:'2026-11-05',updated:'2026-11-05',summary:'Check degree mode, reproduce worked calculations and understand errors before relying on a scientific calculator result.',tools:['calculator','percentage','scientific-notation'],sources:['mathSin','calculatorSource'],sections:[
 {title:'Check the angle unit before entering an expression',paragraphs:['An angle without a unit is easy to misinterpret. Nepocore’s scientific calculator uses degrees for sin, cos and tan, and returns degrees for inverse trigonometric functions. Its DEG label is a statement of that behavior. It is not a switch to radians. If your exercise gives an angle in radians, convert the angle deliberately or use a calculator that supports the required unit.','Start with sin(30). The expected answer in degrees is 0.5. In contrast, the JavaScript Math.sin function documented by MDN takes radians; a degree-based interface must account for that difference. A small known example is a useful check when comparing two programs. A result that differs does not by itself establish that either program is broken: first compare angle units and the expression actually entered.']},
 {title:'Make grouping and multiplication explicit',paragraphs:['Type the complete expression into the Expression field or build it with the keypad. Use parentheses to show which calculation belongs together. Enter (12 + 8) * 3 for 60; entering 12 + 8 * 3 gives 36 because multiplication is evaluated before addition. Both calculations are valid, but they answer different questions.','Use the multiplication key or an explicit * between values. Keeping multiplication visible makes a saved expression easier to check later. After editing a field, calculate again and read the expression shown with the result. Copying an earlier answer without checking the expression can carry a stale value into your work. The calculator is an arithmetic aid, so write down your assumptions separately when solving a word problem.']},
 {title:'Reproduce a short set of reference calculations',paragraphs:['These examples exercise several different controls. Enter each one on its own and compare the result. For the square-root and power examples, the keypad is useful when you do not remember the accepted typed syntax. The More typed functions & examples panel explains additional input forms.'],table:{headers:['Expression or keypad operation','Expected result','What it checks'],rows:[['sin(30)','0.5','Degree input'],['cos(60)','0.5','Degree input'],['2^5','32','Exponentiation'],['sqrt(144)','12','Square root'],['log(1000)','3','Base-10 logarithm'],['5!','120','Factorial']]},paragraphsAfter:['A small difference at the last displayed digit can come from floating-point arithmetic and display rounding. Nepocore displays up to 12 significant digits. That does not mean the underlying mathematical quantity has only 12 digits, or that an approximate input becomes exact because the output looks precise. Keep sufficient intermediate precision for your task and round the final result according to the exercise or measurement requirements.']},
 {title:'Read a domain error as useful information',paragraphs:['Tangent at 90 degrees is undefined. The calculator reports that problem rather than presenting a very large finite approximation as a meaningful answer. Other expressions also have limits: a real square root of a negative number and a logarithm of a non-positive number need a different mathematical domain. This calculator is not a complex-number system.','An error is a reason to inspect the expression, not to delete symbols until a number appears. Check parentheses, angle units, decimal points and the function’s domain. Factorials are bounded to keep calculations practical. Very large or tiny values can be shown in scientific notation; use the notation converter when you need to interpret the exponent.']},
 {title:'Keep percentages, remainders and saved answers distinct',paragraphs:['The percent operation divides a value by 100. For a 15% reduction from 1200, enter 1200 * (1 - 15 / 100), which gives 1020. The mod operation produces a remainder and is not a discount shortcut. Use the percentage calculator when a labeled percent-of or change calculation makes the inputs easier to follow.','Ans refers to the previous answer in the current calculator session. It is convenient for a sequence of operations but is not a permanent notebook or a record synchronized across devices. Record important expressions and independently check results that affect real decisions. These examples explain the tool’s behavior; they do not replace the method, units or reasoning required by your course.']}
]},
{slug:'ielts-overall-band-rounding-worked-examples',title:'Calculate your IELTS overall band: averaging and rounding examples',category:'learning',date:'2026-11-05',updated:'2026-11-05',summary:'Work through four section scores, .25 and .75 boundaries, and the difference between an overall band and a recipient’s requirements.',tools:['ielts-overall','ielts-listening','ielts-reading'],sources:['ieltsScoring'],sections:[
 {title:'Start with four section bands',paragraphs:['The overall calculation uses the awarded Listening, Reading, Writing and Speaking band scores. Add them and divide the total by four. Then round the average to the nearest whole or half band. IELTS publishes the rule, including the upward rounding at averages ending in .25 and .75. Nepocore applies that arithmetic and shows both the average and the rounded overall result.','Enter section bands rather than correct-answer counts. A Listening practice result of 30 out of 40 is a raw mark, not a band of 30. Use a suitable raw-score estimate first if you are working from practice questions. Writing and Speaking also need assessed section bands; counting words or rating your confidence cannot supply an official section score.']},
 {title:'Work through an average ending in .25',paragraphs:['Take Listening 8.0, Reading 7.5, Writing 7.0 and Speaking 6.5. The sum is 29.0. Dividing by four gives 7.25, which rounds upward to an overall band of 7.5. Keep the average visible until the rounding step so you can explain where the final band came from.','Do not round each section again or round 7.25 to a whole number before applying the rule. Section inputs are already band scores. An extra rounding step can change the result and make a correct calculation look inconsistent. Enter the same four values into the calculator and compare its Average before rounding line with your written arithmetic.']},
 {title:'Compare .75 and other boundaries',paragraphs:['For Listening 8.0, Reading 8.0, Writing 7.5 and Speaking 7.5, the total is 31.0 and the average is 7.75. This rounds upward to 8.0. Not every average ends at those boundaries: for example, 6.0, 6.0, 5.5 and 6.0 average 5.875 and round to 6.0.'],table:{headers:['L / R / W / S','Average','Overall band'],rows:[['8.0 / 7.5 / 7.0 / 6.5','7.25','7.5'],['8.0 / 8.0 / 7.5 / 7.5','7.75','8.0'],['7.5 / 7.0 / 6.5 / 7.0','7.0','7.0'],['6.0 / 6.0 / 5.5 / 6.0','5.875','6.0']]},paragraphsAfter:['These are original arithmetic examples, not reported test results or predictions of a learner’s performance. Try changing just one section by half a band to see whether the final overall band changes. A higher average can still round to the same overall band. That is a property of the rounding interval, rather than evidence that improvement in that section has no value.']},
 {title:'Keep overall scores separate from minimum section requirements',paragraphs:['Two people can have the same overall band and different section scores. A university, professional body or immigration route may require a particular overall score and separate minimums in one or more sections. The overall number alone does not establish that the full requirement is met.','Check the receiving organization’s current official wording for the test type, section minimums, accepted test versions and result validity. This tool does not read application rules or make an admission or visa decision. If the wording is unclear, resolve it with the recipient rather than treating a rounded total as permission to apply.']},
 {title:'Use practice estimates honestly',paragraphs:['Practice raw-score conversions are estimates. The score needed for a band can vary with the test version, and Academic and General Training Reading are not interchangeable scales. Keep the original practice paper and mark scheme alongside any converted score so you know what the estimate refers to.','Use the overall calculator to understand the arithmetic and compare scenarios, then plan study around the actual skills you need to improve. It cannot predict an examiner’s future Writing or Speaking assessment. Nepocore is an independent practice tool, not an IELTS Test Report Form or an official score verification service. The linked IELTS reference is the authority for the published scoring rule.']}
]},
{slug:'create-chibi-anime-avatar-transparent-png-svg',title:'Create a chibi anime avatar with transparent PNG and editable SVG',category:'creative',date:'2026-11-05',updated:'2026-11-05',summary:'Choose illustrated parts, build a readable avatar and check transparent PNG or SVG exports without confusing the builder with a photo-to-anime service.',tools:['anime-character','image-cropper','image-resizer'],sources:['builderSource','svgGuide','formats'],sections:[
 {title:'Choose the kind of character you want to make',paragraphs:['Nepocore’s anime character creator combines original illustrated parts into a chibi-style character. You choose a hairstyle, expression, outfit, accessory and colors. It is a hands-on character builder, not a text-prompt image model or a photo-to-anime converter. You do not need to upload a face photograph to use it.','Decide where the character will appear before selecting details. A profile picture needs a recognizable face at a small size. A full-body character for a presentation can use more outfit detail. The exported image is a starting asset: the destination can have its own size, aspect-ratio and file-format requirements, so check those before assuming one download fits every use.']},
 {title:'Build a reproducible first character',paragraphs:['For a simple example, choose Soft bob hair, Bright eyes, Cozy hoodie and no accessory. Set a dark hair color and a contrasting eye and hoodie color, then leave the background on Warm cream while checking the silhouette. Give the character an optional short name only if you want that text in the artwork.','Change one control at a time and watch the preview update. The Surprise me button gives a new combination of parts and colors, which can help you explore, but it is not a way to reproduce a saved design. If you want to rebuild the same character later, record the chosen controls and color values along with your exported files.'],list:['Choose a hairstyle and hair color.','Select an expression and eye color.','Pick the outfit, outfit color and skin tone.','Add an accessory if it remains readable.','Set the background and inspect the final preview.']},
 {title:'Check the avatar at the size people will see',paragraphs:['A detail that looks clear in a large preview can disappear in a small circular profile crop. Check the eyes, hair outline and accessory at the destination size. Strong separation between adjacent colors can help, but no single palette guarantees readability against every website background.','The full character is portrait-shaped. If a service uses a square avatar, make a copy and crop around the face or upper body, then resize the crop. Keep the original full-body export. Cropping is a different operation from stretching: forcing a portrait into a square changes the character’s proportions and can make the face look wider than intended.']},
 {title:'Export a transparent PNG or an SVG',paragraphs:['Select Transparent cutout when you need the character without a colored rectangle. Then download the PNG or SVG and open the actual file to check it. The PNG export is 1800 × 2200 pixels. A transparent region may appear white in an image viewer; testing it over a colored background helps confirm the result.','PNG is a raster image made of pixels. SVG keeps vector shapes and is useful in software that supports editing or scaling them. A service that accepts PNG may reject SVG, so use the format the destination supports. Converting the transparent PNG to JPEG will remove alpha transparency; keep a transparent-capable format when you want the cutout effect.'],table:{headers:['Need','Useful starting file','Check before use'],rows:[['Upload to a typical profile service','PNG','Crop, dimensions and file-size limit'],['Edit vector parts in compatible software','SVG','Application support and text appearance'],['Place a cutout on a presentation','Transparent PNG or supported SVG','Edges and contrast on the actual background']]}},
 {title:'Keep the source design and use characters responsibly',paragraphs:['Save a copy before resizing or flattening an export into another image. A smaller PNG cannot restore detail removed by an earlier crop, while an SVG may preserve editable vector information for a later revision. Open the final exported file and check the character name, colors and background instead of assuming the preview and download are interchangeable.','This tool does not establish identity, verify a person’s likeness or grant rights to someone else’s brand or character. Use original names and combinations, and follow the destination’s rules for avatars. These instructions describe the builder and file formats; they are not a claim that a design has been professionally reviewed or will be accepted by every platform.']}
]}
];
